f"Demand-driven e-waste collection can reduce vehicle visits, but forecast errors are amplified by vehicle-capacity limits when they drive routing decisions. We propose a six-layer architecture (data preparation, forecasting, prioritisation, capacitated routing, dispatch, feedback) and study, by simulation, how forecast uncertainty affects service level and cost (30 collection points, 4 vehicles of capacity 300, a 30-day warm-up followed by a 120-day horizon, 30 paired test instances; hyper-parameters tuned on 30 separate training instances). "
f"With perfect forecasts, demand-driven collection cuts stops by {abs(red('stops')):.1f}%, distance by {abs(red('dist')):.1f}% and cost per collected unit by {abs(red('cpu')):.1f}% relative to the alternating-halves fixed schedule, and overflow loss falls from {q['lost_pct']['orig']:.1f}% to {q['lost_pct']['fc']:.1f}% of the stock-plus-generation. "
