f"An uncertainty buffer trades about {fam(0.5,'Buffered','Naive','dist')['pct']:.0f}% more distance for {abs(fam(0.5,'Buffered','Naive','lost_pct')['diff']):.1f} percentage points less loss at σ = 0.5. Moving-average, random-forest, XGBoost and LSTM forecasters trained on censored simulated logs show measured σ of {min(sef):.2f}–{max(sef):.2f}; none beats the tuned fixed schedule on a cost-plus-loss-penalty objective. "
