add('p', text=f"**Buffered vs naive.** At σ = 0.5 the buffered policy lowers overflow loss from {b05['lost_pct']['mb']:.2f}% to {b05['lost_pct']['ma']:.2f}% (difference {b05['lost_pct']['diff']:+.2f} ± {b05['lost_pct']['ci']:.2f} pp, Holm t p {fp(b05['lost_pct']['pt_holm'])}) but increases distance by {pct(b05['dist']['pct'])} (p {fp(b05['dist']['pt_holm'])}) and cost per collected unit by {pct(b05['cpu']['pct'])} ({b05['cpu']['mb']:.3f} → {b05['cpu']['ma']:.3f}, p {fp(b05['cpu']['pt_holm'])}). At σ = 1.0 the loss reduction is {b10['lost_pct']['diff']:+.2f} pp ({b10['lost_pct']['mb']:.1f}% → {b10['lost_pct']['ma']:.1f}%) for {pct(b10['dist']['pct'])} distance and {pct(b10['cpu']['pct'])} cost per unit. At σ = 0.3 the buffer yields no significant loss reduction ({fam(0.3,'Buffered','Naive','lost_pct')['diff']:+.2f} pp, p {fp(fam(0.3,'Buffered','Naive','lost_pct')['pt_holm'])}) while costing {pct(fam(0.3,'Buffered','Naive','dist')['pct'])} distance. The earlier draft stated that the buffer lowered distance and cost relative to the naive policy; this was an error in sign: the buffer visits more points and always increases distance and cost.")
add('p', text=f"**Buffered vs the paper baseline.** At σ = 0.5 the buffered policy has lower loss ({bo05['lost_pct']['diff']:+.2f} ± {bo05['lost_pct']['ci']:.2f} pp, p {fp(bo05['lost_pct']['pt_holm'])}) and lower cost per unit ({pct(bo05['cpu']['pct'])}, p {fp(bo05['cpu']['pt_holm'])}) with statistically indistinguishable distance ({pct(bo05['dist']['pct'])}, p {fp(bo05['dist']['pt_holm'])}). At σ = 1.0 its cost per unit is still {pct(bo10['cpu']['pct'])} lower (p {fp(bo10['cpu']['pt_holm'])}), but the loss advantage is no longer significant ({bo10['lost_pct']['diff']:+.2f} pp, p {fp(bo10['lost_pct']['pt_holm'])}) and distance is indistinguishable ({pct(bo10['dist']['pct'])}); the cost-per-unit advantage that the draft reported as disappearing at σ = 1.0 (0.183 vs 0.185) is, in the present runs, {bo10['cpu']['ma']:.3f} vs {bo10['cpu']['mb']:.3f}.")
add('p', text=f"**Buffered vs the tuned fixed schedule.** Against the stronger baseline the buffer does not pay: at σ = 0.5 it loses {bt05['lost_pct']['diff']:+.2f} ± {bt05['lost_pct']['ci']:.2f} pp more (p {fp(bt05['lost_pct']['pt_holm'])}), travels {pct(bt05['dist']['pct'])} further and costs {pct(bt05['cpu']['pct'])} more per unit (both p < 0.001). The fill at visit falls with the buffer (Table VIII) because lowered thresholds visit points earlier; this is the price of underestimating, and replaces the unreported ‘62–69%’ claim of the draft.")
